{"kind":"report","text":"Ruling on 9d32984b: the fresh G3 room takes a new register.\n\nThank you for checking the guards before asking Hugh. They settle it.\nThe original home has already claimed the first room, so claim()\nrefuses at its repository guard. retainedRegisterSelector does not\nadmit Register 25. So no supported recipe creates a second room from\nthat home. My rulings 2eb432f9 and b6ea9618 named a path that does not\nexist. They are withdrawn. Do not ask Hugh for the original home.\n\nThe supported path is the one that made the first room on 2 November:\nplan a new register from a new home, deploy, install, then create.\nWith installed registers on main since d7f1ebf7, the earlier registers\nstay listed, so neither H3 nor the first G3 room is stranded.\n\n1. Configuration head, for review: a source export of main at\n   c55c59da or later; github-app.json with registerScope as the one\n   placeholder for the new register; INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES with\n   H3's sc_7prhc2jy..., G3's sc_wktzr3u2... and the new register as a\n   placeholder; bindings.json with the first G3 room's row unchanged;\n   and a new home path, /Users/inguz/dap-host-g3b-20261103/client.\n2. After approval I run the window, as on 2 November: plan with\n   --cohort repository-binding from the new home, fill the two\n   placeholders, stage, deploy, install, and take the four\n   served-bundle readings. The H3 check includes an Inbox birth.\n3. You create the fresh room from the new home with --branch\n   g3-witness-2, write its content, and file the binding-row head for\n   the new Destination.\n4. After that approval, I deploy the binding project, and you bind once\n   and run the witness.\n\nThe failed fresh-owner root and its recovery key stay retained and\nunused. Record in docs/self-host.md that a planned register's client\nhome creates one room, and that another room needs its own plan.\n\nBuilder: please ratify this report by its own ID so 9d32984b closes.","body":{"no_git_arti